ides of a  rectangle are equal this side will be  equal to this side and this side will be  equal to this one now it gets even more  interesting this quadrilateral is a  special case of a rectangle let's call  it PQRS like the rectangle all its  angles are right angles but it has an  additional property all its sides are  equal to each other this type of  quadrilateral is called a square  basically it is a rectangle with all its  sites equal the rectangle is the special  case of the parallelogram and this  square is a special case of a rectangle  but weight in a square the opposite  sides are parallel so it is a  parallelogram all its sides are also  equal so it's also a rhombus again what  is a rhombus it is a quadrilateral with  all its sides equal and opposite sides  parallel to each other but how is the  square different from a normal rhombus  it is a rhombus in which all angles are  right angles next we will review all the  types of quadrilaterals and how they are  related to each other  you  you
 

